{
  "genes": [
    {
      "type": "structure",
      "text": "Search a reflection-symmetric population containing three circles centred on the symmetry axis and nine mirrored pairs. Encode each pair by one centre and radius. Generate independent row arrangements and radius assignments, retain geometrically diverse elites, and periodically release symmetry before full constrained refinement."
    },
    {
      "type": "structure",
      "text": "Perform coordinated contact surgery: identify near-active circle and wall contacts, select connected clusters of three to six contacts, and temporarily permit violations only within each selected cluster. Apply a displacement targeting those contacts, restore all constraints by continuation, and retain distinct feasible contact graphs rather than only immediate score improvements."
    },
    {
      "type": "structure",
      "text": "Use destroy-and-repair moves that remove two to four spatially adjacent circles. Relax the surviving packing, then reinsert the removed circles into different voids using multiple starting radii and centres. Refine all 21 circles jointly and archive the best result from each distinct contact graph."
    },
    {
      "type": "structure",
      "text": "Generate alternative 21-circle families through neighbouring circle counts. Optimize 20-circle packings, insert a small circle into each promising void, and refine. Separately optimize 22-circle packings, delete each of several small or highly constrained circles, and refine the remaining 21. Enforce positive radii throughout the final optimization."
    },
    {
      "type": "formulation",
      "text": "Trace aspect-ratio branches instead of optimizing box shape immediately. Fix width plus height to two, solve at a grid of width-to-height ratios from 0.4 to 2.5, and warm-start neighbouring ratios in both directions. Release the aspect ratio only after collecting local optima from different branches."
    },
    {
      "type": "formulation",
      "text": "Implement sequential inner-approximation LPs over centres, radii, and box dimensions. For each pair, freeze its current unit separation vector and impose that the projected new separation exceeds the sum of radii. Maximize total radius subject to linear wall constraints and a centre trust region; update directions after every accepted step."
    },
    {
      "type": "numeric",
      "text": "Use fixed-centre radius LP dual multipliers to build a local model for moving centres. Weight pair-distance derivatives and wall terms by their dual sensitivities, propose a trust-region step, then resolve the radius LP to measure actual improvement. Reject inaccurate predictions and reduce the trust radius near LP basis changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "numeric",
      "text": "Polish promising packings with an explicit constrained solver using analytic derivatives, rather than ending with a penalty objective. Optimize centres, positive radii, and box width with height equal to two minus width. Enforce every squared-distance and wall inequality, then independently validate the resulting unsquared float distances and exact-Fraction perimeter."
    },
    {
      "type": "structure",
      "text": "Seed searches from mixed-radius lattice families rather than only jittered rectangular grids. Enumerate staggered row-count compositions totalling 21, initialize two or three radius classes, and place smaller circles in inter-row or boundary gaps. Optimize each construction first within its row ordering, then release all ordering constraints."
    },
    {
      "type": "numeric",
      "text": "Replace blanket radius shrinkage with minimum-loss feasibility repair. Recompute pair distances using the verifier's exact floating-point expression, impose conservative pair bounds in a radius LP, and reserve a tiny perimeter margin. Recheck exact Fractions and adjust offending radii with nextafter until valid; measure score loss separately from geometric optimization."
    }
  ]
}
